cat << !ENDMARK >uidprio!3 - History line is not evaluated!c - History match is not evaluatedmd - Aliases are not evaluated-t - Mware syntax is not substitutedThis shell's uid is $$ and its priority is $:!ENDMARKlist uidpriodel uidpriocat << "ENDMARK" >getuidThe shell's uid can be obtained using the $$ symbolENDMARKlist getuiddel getuidcat << \ENDMARK >getprioThe shell's priority can be obtained using the $: symbolENDMARKlist getpriodel getprio